# Candidate kernels under runs/ ARE tracked (so `codex review` / git history see the
# actual kernel source, not just the benchmark.csv / candidates.jsonl evidence rows).
# Only generated/compiled artifacts under runs/ stay ignored (compiled kernels are
# covered by the *.neff / *.ntff / __pycache__ patterns below).
workspaces/*/runs/*
!workspaces/*/runs/*.py
workspaces/*/profile/
workspaces/*/logs/
logs/
outputs/
*.neff
*.ntff
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.humanize/

# .claude/skills/ holds placeholder skill folders (tracked). Their real contents
# live in a separate NKI kernel library not shipped here; drop them in or symlink
# per the snippet in README. Ignore any local symlink/build artifacts inside.
.claude/skills/*/SKILL.md

# Per-op prompt files are generated from prompts/_gen_prompts.py (benchmark-derived
# content is not checked in); regenerate locally with `python3 prompts/_gen_prompts.py`.
prompts/*/phase*.md
